<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48457" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tītyrus</span></b> , i,
			m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>the name of a shepherd
				in Virgil</i>'<i>s Eclogues</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. E.
			1</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> For <i>a
				shepherd</i> in gen., <i><span class="en">Verg. E. 8,
			55</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			As a designation of <i>Virgil</i>'<i>s
				Eclogues</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. Am. 1, 15, 25</span></i>. —
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b> As a designation of
				<i>Virgil</i> himself, <i><span class="en">Prop. 2,
			34</span></i> (3, 32), 72.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>